<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aleut</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Unangan, Aleut people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aleut, or Unangan, are the Indigenous people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleutian-islands">Aleutian Islands</a> and the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a> Peninsula, skilled sea hunters in skin kayaks. From the 1740s Russian fur traders forced them to hunt sea otters, and violence and disease greatly reduced their numbers. Many converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox Christianity</a>, which remains strong among them.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aleut.jpg" alt="Aleut" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Malcolm Greany · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greany_Attu_Woman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
